Package: linuxscp
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, python3
Recommends: curl
Description: graphical and console file transfer client for Linux
 LinSCP is a native open-source file transfer client for Linux, inspired
 by WinSCP. It provides an interactive command-line client (linuxscp) and
 a dual-pane Commander graphical client (linuxscp-gui) in the browser.
 .
 SFTP is served by the bundled PuTTY core; scp, ftp, ftps, WebDAV and S3
 go through curl, which is why it is recommended. The client provides
 transfer resume and recursive synchronization, public-key, ssh-agent and
 password authentication, host-key verification, stored sessions and a
 subset of WinSCP scripting. Protocol support depends on the backend;
 WebDAV and Amazon S3 support are incomplete. Full WinSCP feature parity
 is not provided.
